<title>SWITZERLAND: Central bankers no comment on Greenspan policy.</title>
<headline>Central bankers no comment on Greenspan policy.</headline>
<dateline>INTERLAKEN, Switzerland 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of England governor Eddie George said central bankers meeting at a banking conference in Interlaken in Switzerland would not comment on the policy of U.S. Federal Reserve chief Alan Greenspan.</p>
<p>George was speaking on behalf of a panel of central bank governors at the meeting.  </p>
<p>Asked at a briefing what Greenspan had told commercial and central bankers about U.S. monetary policy, George said:</p>
<p>&quot;No one would dare to comment on the U.S. perspective.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Peter Nielsen, Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
